TitanOS Revenue & Fee System (Production Architecture)

You are the Lead Software Architect for TitanOS.

Design and implement a centralized, configurable fee management system for
the platform.
Primary Goal

Every transaction, service, subscription, commission, and payment must use
one centralized pricing engine.

No fee percentages, flat fees, or commission rates should ever be hardcoded
into business logic or UI components.
------------------------------
Requirements

Create a Fee Engine responsible for calculating all platform fees.

The Fee Engine should support:

   -

   Percentage fees
   -

   Flat fees
   -

   Minimum fees
   -

   Maximum fees
   -

   Tiered pricing
   -

   Promotional discounts
   -

   Coupons
   -

   Taxes (optional)
   -

   Future expansion

All fee calculations must come from a single source of truth.
------------------------------
Configuration

Store fee configuration in one secure location (database or configuration
layer).

Example categories:

Marketplace Sales

Driver Services

Service Requests

Subscriptions

Premium Membership

Featured Listings

Promoted Posts

Advertising

Future Products

Each category should have independently configurable pricing.
------------------------------
Administrative Controls

Create an Admin Fee Management page where authorized administrators can:

   -

   Change fee percentages
   -

   Enable or disable fees
   -

   Add new fee categories
   -

   Schedule future fee changes
   -

   View fee history
   -

   Roll back changes if necessary

No code changes should be required to update pricing.
------------------------------
Fee Calculation

For every transaction:

Calculate:

Gross Amount

Platform Fee

Processing Fee (if applicable)

Taxes (if enabled)

Net Amount

Final Customer Total

All calculations should be transparent and auditable.
------------------------------
Reporting

Record every fee calculation.

Store:

Transaction ID

Fee Version

Calculation Timestamp

Fee Category

Applied Rules

Gross Amount

Platform Fee

Net Amount

Final Total

This creates a complete audit trail.
------------------------------
Security

Never trust client-side calculations.

All fee calculations must occur securely on the server.

Validate all incoming payment amounts.

Prevent manipulation of pricing from the browser.
------------------------------
Scalability

The architecture must support future additions such as:

   -

   Different fees by country
   -

   Different fees by user role
   -

   Seasonal promotions
   -

   Referral discounts
   -

   Enterprise pricing
   -

   Membership discounts
   -

   Volume pricing
   -

   Loyalty rewards

without requiring a major rewrite.
------------------------------
Performance

Cache fee configurations when appropriate.

Avoid unnecessary database queries.

Ensure fee calculations remain fast even at high transaction volume.
------------------------------
Maintainability

Every pricing rule must be:

   -

   Documented
   -

   Modular
   -

   Testable
   -

   Easy to extend

Avoid duplicated pricing logic.
------------------------------
Testing

Create automated tests covering:

   -

   Percentage fees
   -

   Flat fees
   -

   Minimum fees
   -

   Maximum fees
   -

   Edge cases
   -

   Invalid inputs
   -

   Large transactions
   -

   Small transactions

------------------------------
Final Goal

TitanOS should have a production-ready, centralized revenue system that is
secure, configurable, auditable, and flexible enough to support future
business models without changing core application code.

